{% comment %}
  Accordion row — one collapsible panel.

  Built on <details>/<summary>, so it opens, closes, takes focus and responds to
  Enter and Space with no JavaScript at all, and its content is still findable
  by in-page search in browsers that support it.

  Call it once per row and wrap the calls in a container carrying the
  `accordion` class so the rows share their dividers:

    <div class="accordion">
      {% render 'accordion-item', id: 'x-1', title: 'First', content: '<p>…</p>' %}
      {% render 'accordion-item', id: 'x-2', title: 'Second', content: '<p>…</p>' %}
    </div>

  Requires assets/component-accordion-item.css.

  Accepts:
  - title: {String} the row's label. Required — a row with no label cannot be
    opened meaningfully.
  - content: {String} the row's HTML body. Required.
  - id: {String} unique id for the row, so a link can address it.
  - open: {Boolean} render the row already expanded (optional, default false).
  - group: {String} shared name so opening one row closes the others in that
    group (optional).

  Usage:
  {% render 'accordion-item', id: 'faq-1', title: 'Do you ship abroad?',
    content: block.settings.answer %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- if title != blank and content != blank -%}
  <details
    class="accordion-item"
    {% if id != blank %}
      id="{{ id }}"
    {% endif %}
    {% if group != blank %}
      name="{{ group }}"
    {% endif %}
    {% if open %}
      open
    {% endif %}
  >
    <summary class="accordion-item__summary">
      <span class="accordion-item__title">{{ title }}</span>
      <span class="accordion-item__icon svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="accordion-item__panel">
      <div class="accordion-item__content rte">{{ content }}</div>
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
